<Prose
  locale="en"
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy: OpenShuttle collects no data"
  description="The OpenShuttle app collects and sends no data. The openshuttle.app website uses no cookies and measures its audience without personal tracking."
  heading="Privacy"
  lead="Your tournaments and your players’ names never leave your computer."
  updated="2026-10-20"
>
  <h2>The OpenShuttle app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No data collected.</strong> OpenShuttle runs fully offline. It makes no network connection, sends no usage statistics or
      crash reports, and does not check for updates online.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your data stays with you.</strong> Tournaments (entrants, clubs, scores, history) are saved in <code>.openshuttle</code>
      files on your computer, with backup copies in the same place. Settings, presets and the club list live in a local app file.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You are in charge.</strong> As the organizer, you are the one handling players’ names: keep the files safe and delete
      them when you no longer need them. CSV exports and archives are only created when you ask, where you choose.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The openshuttle.app website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No cookies</strong>, no accounts, no forms, no ads.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare Workers. Like any host, Cloudflare processes technical connection data
      (IP address, browser, requested page) to deliver the pages and protect the site, under its
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Audience measurement.</strong> When enabled, audience measurement uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, with no cookies and no
      browser fingerprinting: it counts visits in aggregate, without following people across sites.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Downloads.</strong> Download links redirect to files published on GitHub, covered by the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Fonts are hosted on the site itself: no request to Google Fonts or any other third party.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    The site keeps no personal data about you, so there is nothing to access or delete on our side. For any question, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or open an issue on <a href={github.issues}>GitHub</a>. See also the
    <a href={routes.legal.en}>legal notice</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
